   <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AITEO</td>\n                <td>₦1,610.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Crash 5% as Markets Bet on US-Iran Deal Despite Hormuz Threats\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was trading at $79.39 per barrel, down 5.23%, while US West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude stood at $75.86 per barrel. The renewed weakness in crude prices followed comments from US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and Qatar's Foreign Ministry suggesting that progress was being made on a draft framework.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-crash-5-as-markets-bet-on-us-iran-deal-despite-hormuz-threats\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Begins Approval Process for 1.6 Million-Barrel Namibia Fuel Depot\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Dangote Industries Namibia Ltd has applied for an Environmental Clearance Certificate (ECC) for the subdivision of about 70 hectares of industrial land on Farm 58 in Walvis Bay. The proposed development is expected to strengthen Namibia's strategic fuel storage capacity. The project forms part of Dangote's broader African expansion strategy.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-begins-approval-process-for-16-million-barrel-namibia-fuel-depot\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Hormuz Tanker Traffic Stays Weak Despite Trump's Peace Claims\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Only three oil tankers transited the Strait of Hormuz on Monday, down from seven vessels recorded on Sunday. In the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, 12 tankers made the crossing, with most vessels keeping their transponders switched on. The subdued shipping activity suggests that concerns over security in the region continue to outweigh optimism generated by Trump's comments.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/hormuz-tanker-traffic-stays-weak-despite-trumps-peace-claims\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Refinery Weighs Fuel Price Review as Market Conditions Shift — Sources\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Dangote Petroleum Refinery is considering a review of its petrol and diesel prices as it evaluates prevailing market conditions. The development comes as international crude oil prices continue to soften.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-refinery-weighs-fuel-price-review-as-market-conditions-shift-sources\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Nigeria Targets End to Crude Exports as Local Refining Capacity Surges\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Federal Government has unveiled plans to gradually phase out crude oil exports as Nigeria ramps up domestic refining capacity. The Chief Executive of the Nigerian Midstream and Downstream Petroleum Regulatory Authority, Rabiu Umar, disclosed the strategy on Monday. He said the country’s expanding refining infrastructure, driven by large-scale private investments and modular refineries, could transform Nigeria into Africa's leading refining hub.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nigeria-targets-end-to-crude-exports-as-local-refining-capacity-surges\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
